# {{ name }}

A [Nesto](https://github.com/trynesto/framework) application

## Install

```bash
composer install
cp .env.example .env   # `nesto new` already created .env
```

## Run

```bash
# development server (PHP built-in server, serves public/)
php nesto start --port=3000
# or without the CLI
php -S 127.0.0.1:3000 -t public public/index.php
```

Then open http://127.0.0.1:3000/api — you should see `Hello World!`.

## Configure

Everything is driven by `.env` (each key is documented there) and `config/*.php`:

| Key | Values |
| --- | --- |
| `ORM_DRIVER` | `orm` (entities + repositories), `prisma` (prisma/schema.prisma), `none` |
| `DB_CONNECTION`, `DB_DATABASE`, `DB_HOST`… | the database (`sqlite`, `mysql`, `mariadb`, `pgsql`) |
| `CACHE_DRIVER` | `memory`, `file`, `database`, `redis` (`REDIS_HOST`, `REDIS_PORT`…) |
| `LOG_CHANNEL`, `LOG_PATH`, `LOG_LEVEL`, `LOG_DAILY` | where errors and logs go (default `storage/logs/nesto.log` + stderr) |

`php nesto info` shows what is in effect; `php nesto cache:clear` empties the cache.

## Test

```bash
vendor/bin/phpunit
```

## Generate code

```bash
php nesto g resource cats        # module + controller + service + DTOs + entity
php nesto g controller cats      # auto-registered in src/Cats/CatsModule.php
php nesto g service cats
php nesto routes                 # list every route
php nesto --help
```
